%% Historical fast(-but-wrong) path — behavior BEFORE commit e61fcb11
%% "Attach Filtered Tree Walk Optimization to Fastpath Switch" (2026-06-23 08:31 UTC).
%% This is the read-only Stage/Diff/Patch filtered-retrieval flow as it behaved while
%% ZCL_ABAPGIT_ORTEC_FILTER_WALK was called UNCONDITIONALLY (no feature-switch gate),
%% relying only on cached-state validity to decide fast vs. fallback.
flowchart TD
  A[User opens Stage / Diff / Patch with an object filter] --> B[ZCL_ABAPGIT_STAGE_LOGIC / ZCL_ABAPGIT_GUI_PAGE_DIFF_BASE.get_files_and_status]
  B --> C{Object filter present?}
  C -->|No| D[Full ii_repo_online->get_files_remote]
  C -->|Yes, historical code| E["CALL METHOD ZCL_ABAPGIT_ORTEC_FILTER_WALK=>GET_REMOTE_FILES_FOR_STAGE / DIFF (always attempted, no switch check)"]

  E --> F[Resolve repo_key via SHA1 hash of URL against ZAOG_REPO_STATE]
  F --> G{repo_key found?}
  G -->|No| D
  G -->|Yes| H[Read ZAOG_REPO_STATE fetch_commit for selected branch]
  H --> I{fetch_commit cached AND branch tip still matches remote HEAD}
  I -->|No / stale| D
  I -->|Yes, valid cache| J[ZCL_ABAPGIT_ORTEC_OBJ_INDEX.get_files_for_filter: sparse lookup against ZAOG_OBJ_INDEX / ZAOG_OBJ_STORE, only touches filtered obj_type/obj_name rows]
  J --> K[Return small filtered remote file set fast, independent of repo size]

  D --> L[zcl_abapgit_repo_status=>calculate over full remote+local sets]
  K --> L
  L --> M[Render Stage / Diff / Patch page]

  classDef fast fill:#dfffe0,stroke:#2f9e44;
  classDef slow fill:#ffe3e3,stroke:#c92a2a;
  class E,F,G,H,I,J,K fast
  class D,B slow

  %% Key property (confirmed by source + git blame, not an assumption):
  %% - Fast path was reachable for ANY filtered request as long as valid state existed,
  %%   with no per-user/per-repo opt-in toggle in front of it.
  %% - The only gates were data-validity gates (repo_key exists, fetch_commit exists,
  %%   branch tip unchanged) -- never a policy/feature-switch gate.
  %% - The mutating pull path (ZCL_ABAPGIT_ORTEC_FASTPATH, writes to ZAOG_*) was ALREADY
  %%   opt-in gated by ZCL_ABAPGIT_ORTEC_GIT_SWITCH=>IS_ACTIVE_FOR_REPO since commit
  %%   3e964850 (2026-05-13) / 81345469 (2026-05-28). That gating is unrelated to this
  %%   diagram and is classified separately as "required, must be preserved".
